# Long Road Architecture

Oregon Trail–style trail simulation. Code lives in assembly-defined layers under `Assets/_Game/` and `Assets/Packages/`.

## Layers

- **LongRoad.Domain** (`Assets/_Game/LongRoad.Domain`) — pure C#, `noEngineReferences`. Party, journey, resources, events, rules.
- **LongRoad.Core** (`Assets/_Game/LongRoad.Core`) — Unity adapters/services referencing Domain (+ Packages).
- **LongRoad** (`Assets/_Game/LongRoad`) — MonoBehaviours, UI, scenes wiring; references Domain, Core, Packages.
- **LongRoad.Packages** (`Assets/Packages`) — local/third-party code; never depends on game assemblies.

## Dependency rule

`Domain` is isolated (no Unity / no Packages). `Core` and `LongRoad` may use Domain and Packages. Packages never depends on game code.

## Placement

| Put here | Examples |
|----------|----------|
| Domain | Trail progress, rationing, event resolution, win/lose |
| Core | Save adapters, time/clock bridges, DI/facades over Domain |
| LongRoad | UI screens, input handlers, audio, scene controllers |
| Packages | Vendored utilities unrelated to Long Road rules |

Prefer Domain logic + thin Unity wrappers over fat MonoBehaviours.
